reply.body:
Do you mean [this](https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/look-and-feel/autosizing-textview)? That's only supported on Android 8 and newer.

`progressCurrentTime` and `progressEndTime` need to have the same size which centers the seekbar automatically. 
What I meant, is this:
``` JAVA
if (currentTimeParams.getWidth() > progressEndTime.getWidth()) {
     endTimeParams.width = progressCurrentTime.getWidth();
} else {
     currentTimeParams.width = progressEndTime.getWidth();
}
```
But I guess there is a proper way to do this by using a linear layout/constaint layout and layout weight.

@Stypox How would you do this?

> theoretically currentTime width is never bigger than endTime's, 

@Stypox 
It is only bigger when listening to normal streams. When listening to a livestream, the right view just says _LIVE_ (see the screenshots above). For this reason the view for the current position is that small atm.
